    "math_academy_id": "q-124143",
    "knowledge_point_id": "8ba09dd1-d219-5df2-adfa-d88d7b9fc481",
    "knowledge_point": "Finding the Image of a Point or Segment",
    "problem": "Consider the transformation $T$ defined as\n\n$$\nx=2u-v,\\,y=u+3v-1.\n$$\n\nLet $P(2,-2)$ be a point in the $uv$-plane. Suppose that the image of $P$ under the action of $T$ is the point ${P}^{′}$ in the $xy$-plane. What are the coordinates of ${P}^{′}?$",
    "worked_solution": "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nNotice that the given transformation can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2u-v \\\\ u+3v-1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2u-v \\\\ u+3v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the image of $P$ under the action of $T,$ we first create a column vector $u$ containing the coordinates of $P:$\n\n$$\nu=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nApplying $T$ to $u,$ we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of ${P}^{′}$ are $(6,-5).$",
